itten as digital ones and zeros.", "reference": "2007 September 11, John Markoff, “Redefining the Architecture of Memory”, in The New York Times, archived from the original on 09 Nov 2020:"}, {"text": "Here is the formal definition: an autobiographical number is a number N such that the first digit of N counts how many zeroes are in N, the second digit counts how many ones are in N and so on. In our example, 1210 has 1 zero, 2 ones, 1 two and 0 threes.", "reference": "2008 March 2, Tanya Khovanova, “Autobiographical Numbers”, in arXiv, page 1:"}, {"text": "This effectively allows switching on and off of the flow of current, so it is either conducting or not conducting, creating the binary system of zeroes and ones used in digital computers.", "reference": "2024 January 4, Matthew Sparkes, “First working graphene semiconductor could lead to faster computers”, in New Scientist, retrieved 18 Jan 2024:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal, uncountable) Nothing, or none.", "tags": ["informal", "uncountable"], "examples": ["The shipment was lost, so they had zero in stock.", "He knows zero about humour.", "In the end, all of our hard work amounted to zero."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "res"}, {"language": {"code": "ceb", "name": "Cebuano"}, "word": "wala"}, {"language": {"code": "ceb", "name": "Cebuano"}, "word": "nulo"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "nic"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "nul"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "ingenting"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "nul"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "nulo"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "ei mitään"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Null"}, {"language": {"code": "hi", "name": "Hindi"}, "wo